/**
 * @defgroup MCC_BuildGuide Build Guide
 * @brief Configure MCC against a matching Foundation package.
 *
 * MCC locates or fetches Foundation automatically (see
 * @ref MCC_BuildGuide_Dependency):
 *
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./scripts/configure.sh macos_arm64 --fresh
 * ./scripts/build.sh macos_arm64 --config Debug
 * @endcode
 *
 * To use a specific Foundation package, point MCC at its prefix:
 *
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./scripts/configure.sh macos_arm64 --fresh -- \
 *   -DMCC_FOUNDATION_PREFIX=../Foundation/dist/macos_arm64
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section MCCBuildGuideLanguage Language Standard
 *
 * CMake packages and direct source builds require C++17. Arduino source mode
 * also supports the C++11 default selected by stock cores, including the AVR
 * core used by Arduino Uno; no global compiler-flag override is required.
 *
 * Functions that require C++14 relaxed `constexpr` are ordinary inline
 * functions only under Arduino C++11. They keep the same runtime behavior and
 * remain `constexpr` with C++14 or newer. Scale and chord catalogs are stored
 * as precomputed constant data, so AVR continues to keep them in program
 * memory rather than initializing them in RAM.
 *
 * The Arduino source-mode gate compiles every example with the core's default
 * flags:
 *
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./scripts/test-arduino.sh
 * @endcode
 *
 * On Windows, run `scripts/test-arduino.ps1` from PowerShell.
 */
